      "summary": {
        "headline": "Transactions and bill payment: published values for FY2020 and how they moved.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "In FY2020, Share of bills paid by mail was 21.0 (percent). That fell by 2.0 percentage points from the previous year, FY2019. That fell by 10.0 percentage points from five years earlier, FY2015.",
            "metric": "bills-paid-by-mail-share",
            "years": [
              2020,
              2019,
              2015
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "In FY2020, Share of bills paid electronically was 76.0 (percent). That rose by 3.0 percentage points from the previous year, FY2019. That rose by 11.0 percentage points from five years earlier, FY2015.",
            "metric": "bills-paid-electronic-share",
            "years": [
              2020,
              2019,
              2015
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "In FY2020, First-Class transaction mail received was 16,728 (millions of pieces). That fell by 503 (2.9%) from the previous year, FY2019. That fell by 4,153 (19.9%) from five years earlier, FY2015.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-transactions",
            "years": [
              2020,
              2019,
              2015
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "In FY2020, First-Class transaction mail sent was 2,940 (millions of pieces). That fell by 234 (7.4%) from the previous year, FY2019. That fell by 1,954 (39.9%) from five years earlier, FY2015.",
            "metric": "fcm-sent-transactions",
            "years": [
              2020,
              2019,
              2015
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "In FY2020, Transaction mail per household was 141.2 (pieces per household per year). That fell by 17.9 (11.3%) from the previous year, FY2019. That fell by 48.3 (25.5%) from five years earlier, FY2015.",
            "metric": "transactions-per-household",
            "years": [
              2020,
              2019,
              2015
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "In FY2020, Transactions mail received per household was 130.0 (pieces per household per year). That fell by 5.2 (3.8%) from the previous year, FY2019. That fell by 52.0 (28.6%) from five years earlier, FY2015.",
            "metric": "transactions-received-per-household",
            "years": [
              2020,
              2019,
              2015
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
          "Methodology change in FY2017: Correspondence/transactions split reclassified (FY2017 report). Comparisons across it should be cautious."
        ]
      },
