      "summary": {
        "headline": "Transactions and bill payment: long-term change in the published values, FY2000 to FY2025.",
        "statements": [
          {
            "text": "Share of bills paid by mail (percent) went from 81.0 in FY2000 to 14.0 in FY2025: it fell by 67.0 percentage points over the period. Since FY2020 (five years earlier) it fell by 7.0 percentage points. Since FY2015 (ten years earlier) it fell by 17.0 percentage points.",
            "metric": "bills-paid-by-mail-share",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2025,
              2020,
              2015
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Projection, not a published figure: the Drift model, fitted on FY2010 to FY2025, puts Share of bills paid by mail at 3.0 in FY2030 (80% range 0.0 to 9.6). On past years it beat the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "bills-paid-by-mail-share",
            "years": [
              2025,
              2030
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Share of bills paid electronically (percent) went from 11.0 in FY2000 to 85.0 in FY2024: it rose by 74.0 percentage points over the period. Since FY2019 (five years earlier) it rose by 12.0 percentage points. Since FY2014 (ten years earlier) it rose by 23.0 percentage points.",
            "metric": "bills-paid-electronic-share",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2024,
              2019,
              2014
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Projection, not a published figure: the Drift model, fitted on FY2010 to FY2024, puts Share of bills paid electronically at 98.2 in FY2029 (80% range 92.5 to 100.0). On past years it beat the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "bills-paid-electronic-share",
            "years": [
              2024,
              2029
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "First-Class transaction mail received (millions of pieces) went from 24,514 in FY2000 to 14,879 in FY2023: it fell by 9,635 (39.3%) over the period. Since FY2018 (five years earlier) it fell by 4,017 (21.3%). Since FY2013 (ten years earlier) it fell by 6,633 (30.8%).",
            "metric": "fcm-received-transactions",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2023,
              2018,
              2013
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Projection, not a published figure: the Holt's exponential smoothing model, fitted on FY2010 to FY2023, puts First-Class transaction mail received at 11,387 in FY2028 (80% range 9,454 to 13,320). On past years it beat the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "fcm-received-transactions",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2028
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "First-Class transaction mail sent (millions of pieces) went from 9,468 in FY2000 to 2,097 in FY2023: it fell by 7,371 (77.9%) over the period. Since FY2018 (five years earlier) it fell by 1,411 (40.2%). Since FY2013 (ten years earlier) it fell by 2,992 (58.8%).",
            "metric": "fcm-sent-transactions",
            "years": [
              2000,
              2023,
              2018,
              2013
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Projection, not a published figure: the Linear trend model, fitted on FY2010 to FY2023, puts First-Class transaction mail sent at 303 in FY2028 (80% range 0 to 677). On past years it beat the naive baseline.",
            "metric": "fcm-sent-transactions",
            "years": [
              2023,
              2028
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Transaction mail per household (pieces per household per year) went from 214.7 in FY2014 to 93.7 in FY2025: it fell by 121.0 (56.4%) over the period. Since FY2020 (five years earlier) it fell by 47.5 (33.6%). Since FY2015 (ten years earlier) it fell by 95.8 (50.6%).",
            "metric": "transactions-per-household",
            "years": [
              2014,
              2025,
              2020,
              2015
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Transactions mail received per household (pieces per household per year) went from 275.6 in FY2003 to 114.4 in FY2023: it fell by 161.2 (58.5%) over the period. Since FY2018 (five years earlier) it fell by 31.2 (21.4%). Since FY2013 (ten years earlier) it fell by 104.0 (47.6%).",
            "metric": "transactions-received-per-household",
            "years": [
              2003,
              2023,
              2018,
              2013
            ]
          }
        ],
        "caveats": [
          "Methodology change in FY2010: Diary data restated with new weighting. Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Methodology change in FY2024: New contractor and per-household reporting. Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "Methodology change in FY2025: Household Mail Survey redesign. Comparisons across it should be cautious.",
          "No projection is shown for Transaction mail per household: Projections need at least 8 consecutive annual values; this series has fewer, so none is shown.",
          "Transaction mail per household has no published value for some years in between, so gaps are left as gaps.",
